A line sloping **up** to the right has a **positive** gradient and an **acute** angle of inclination ($0^{\circ}<\theta<90^{\circ}$).

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{angles, quotes}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (X) at (1.4,0);
\coordinate (P) at (55:2.6);
\coordinate (Q) at (55:-2.6);
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-3,0)--(3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (0,-3)--(0,3) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[blue, thick] (Q)--(P);
\pic[draw, "$\theta$", angle radius=0.85cm, angle eccentricity=1.9] {angle=X--O--P};
\node at (2.05,-1.9) {$m>0$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A line sloping **down** to the right has a **negative** gradient and an **obtuse** angle of inclination ($90^{\circ}<\theta<180^{\circ}$).

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
